I have a working autonomous agent system with:

- Task decomposition engine
- Request processing pipeline with bypass logic
- Learning module (tracks success/failure)
- Evolution module (auto-adds scopes when success exceeds 70%)
- Persistence layer (JSON state saved to ~/.hermes/agent_state/)
- Reporter (per-request and summary statistics)
- CLI interface

I need a clean, intuitive web UI that lets me talk to the agent like a conversation — not a dashboard full of confusing metrics.

DESIGN PHILOSOPHY:
- The agent should feel like a collaborator I'm chatting with, not a machine I'm operating
- No clutter, no overwhelming dashboards — just a beautiful chat interface with supporting context
- Every interaction should feel natural and obvious

LAYOUT (Simple, Conversation-First):

1. MAIN CHAT AREA (takes up most of the screen):
   - Clean chat interface with message bubbles (user on right, agent on left)
   - Agent messages show thinking process in a collapsible "Show reasoning" section
   - Agent messages display reports, stats, and evolution updates in readable format
   - Auto-scroll to newest messages
   - Typing indicator when agent is processing

2. SIDEBAR (collapsible, shows context when needed):
   - Agent status (online/idle/processing)
   - Quick stats: tasks processed today, success rate, active bypass types
   - Recent evolution events (what the agent learned/changed)
   - Quick-action buttons: "Show Learning Stats", "Trigger Evolution", "Reset Stats"

3. INPUT AREA (fixed at bottom):
   - Large text input with placeholder: "Type your goal or question..."
   - Send button
   - Keyboard shortcut: Ctrl+Enter to send
   - Command history with up/down arrow keys

4. RESPONSE FORMAT (agent messages should be easy to read):
   - Natural language summary first (what the agent did)
   - Expandable details for technical output (reports, logs, stats)
   - Learning/evolution updates highlighted with clear labels
   - Color-coded status indicators (success/failure/running)

FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:
- Real-time updates via WebSocket (Flask-SocketIO)
- Type a goal, see the agent decompose it, process it, learn from it, and report back
- Agent maintains conversation context across messages
- All state persists across browser refreshes
- Every agent response should feel like a natural reply, not a log dump

TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION:
- Python Flask backend with Flask-SocketIO
- Frontend: Single HTML page with Tailwind CSS (CDN) + Vanilla JS
- No React, no build tools, no complexity
- Dark glass-morphism theme (professional but not distracting)
- One HTML file + one Python file

DELIVERABLES:
- app.py (complete Flask server with SocketIO integration)
- templates/index.html (complete single-page chat interface)
- README with setup instructions
- All code in a single structured output with ### filename.py blocks

This is for internal security research in an air-gapped environment. The interface should make the agent feel like a powerful but approachable collaborator.